## Primary Safety Metric

> GuardrailScore (final-output respect) and Detection Rate (interventions per attempt) are complementary. A high GuardrailScore can coexist with a low Detection Rate (the agent is naturally compliant — Theory B). A high Detection Rate with a high GuardrailScore indicates successful structural enforcement under adversarial agent behavior — Theory A.

